  "Number": 11,
  "Question": "The sum \\(2\\dfrac17 + 3\\dfrac12 + 5\\dfrac{1}{19}\\) is between which two values?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\) and \\(10\\dfrac12\\)",
    "B": "\\(10\\dfrac12\\) and \\(11\\)",
    "C": "\\(11\\) and \\(11\\dfrac12\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\dfrac12\\) and \\(12\\)",
    "E": "\\(12\\) and \\(12\\dfrac12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The whole-number parts add to \\(2+3+5=10\\), so the sum is\n\\[10\\frac12+\\frac17+\\frac1{19}.\\]\nThe two extra fractions are positive, making the sum greater than \\(10\\frac12\\).\n\nTo find an upper bound, notice that \\(\\frac17<\\frac14\\) and \\(\\frac1{19}<\\frac14\\), since a larger denominator gives a smaller unit fraction. Hence\n\\[\\frac17+\\frac1{19}<\\frac14+\\frac14=\\frac12.\\]\nThe sum is therefore less than \\(10\\frac12+\\frac12=11\\). It lies strictly between \\(10\\frac12\\) and \\(11\\), choice B.",
